<title>FRANCE: CDF issues 1.5 bln Ffr 6.60 pct 2007 bond.</title>
<headline>CDF issues 1.5 bln Ffr 6.60 pct 2007 bond.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following domestic French franc bond was announced by joint lead managers Credit Commercial de France and Caisse Centrale des Banques Populaires.</p>
<p>BORROWER - CHARBONNAGES DE FRANCE (CDF)</p>
<p> AMT   1.5 BLN FRF	COUPON     6.60	MATURITY 25.APR.07</p>
<p> TYPE  STRAIGHT	   ISS PRICE  101.85    PAY DATE 02.OCT.96</p>
<p>				REOFFER    100.90    ACCRUAL  02.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  130 BP	YLD/SPREAD 6.36/+10</p>
<p>NOTE - Yield spread calculated over 6.50 percent 2006 OAT. Bond will be fungible with two billion franc 6.60 percent 2007 CDF issue on July 8.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
